{"name":"Diesel","hex":"#322c2b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"diesel","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fuel derived from petroleum (or other oils) but heavier than gasoline/petrol. Used to power diesel engines which burn this fuel using the heat produced when air is compressed.","A vehicle powered by a diesel engine."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To ignite a substance by using the heat generated by compression.","For a spark-ignition internal combustion engine to continue running after the electrical current to the spark plugs has been turned off. This occurs when there's enough heat in the combustion chamber to ignite the air and fuel mixture without a spark, the same way that heat and pressure cause ignition in a diesel engine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diesel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Diesel engine","blocks":[{"text":"A diesel engine is an internal combustion engine in which ignition of diesel fuel is caused by the elevated temperature of the air in the cylinder due to mechanical compression; thus, the diesel engine is also called a compression-ignition engine. This contrasts with engines using spark plug-ignition of the air-fuel mixture, such as a petrol engine or a gas engine. The diesel engine is named after its inventor, German engineer Rudolf Diesel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/The_Diesel_Story.ogv/250px--The_Diesel_Story.ogv.jpg","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diesel_engine"},{"title":"Diesel fuel","blocks":[{"text":"Diesel fuel, also called diesel oil, fuel oil (historically), or simply diesel, is any liquid fuel specifically designed for use in a diesel engine, a type of internal combustion engine in which fuel ignition takes place as a result of compression of the inlet air and then injection of fuel without a spark. Therefore, diesel fuel needs good compression ignition characteristics."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Red_diesel_tank.jpg/330px-Red_diesel_tank.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diesel_fuel"},{"title":"Diesel (company)","blocks":[{"text":"Diesel S.p.A. is a retail brand headquartered in Breganze, Italy known for luxury denim which also vends clothing, footwear, and accessories. It is part of OTB Group."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Diesel.svg/330px-Diesel.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diesel_(company)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Lumbar_patent_dieselengine.jpg/500px-Lumbar_patent_dieselengine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Lumbar_patent_dieselengine.jpg/1280px-Lumbar_patent_dieselengine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Lumbar_patent_dieselengine.jpg/500px-Lumbar_patent_dieselengine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rudolf Diesel's 1893 patent on a rational heat motor","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALumbar_patent_dieselengine.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Experimental_Diesel_Engine.jpg/500px-Experimental_Diesel_Engine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Experimental_Diesel_Engine.jpg/1280px-Experimental_Diesel_Engine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Experimental_Diesel_Engine.jpg/500px-Experimental_Diesel_Engine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Diesel's second prototype. It is a modification of the first experimental engine. On 17 February 1894, this engine ran under its own power for the first time.[10]Effective efficiency 16.6% Fuel consumption 519 g·kW−1·h−1","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AExperimental_Diesel_Engine.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Historical_Diesel_engine_in_Deutsches_Museum.jpg/500px-Historical_Diesel_engine_in_Deutsches_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Historical_Diesel_engine_in_Deutsches_Museum.jpg/1280px-Historical_Diesel_engine_in_Deutsches_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Historical_Diesel_engine_in_Deutsches_Museum.jpg/500px-Historical_Diesel_engine_in_Deutsches_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"First fully functional diesel engine, designed by Imanuel Lauster, built from scratch, and finished by October 1896.[31][32][33]Rated power 13.1 kWEffective efficiency 26.2% Fuel consumption 324 g·kW−1·h−1.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHistorical_Diesel_engine_in_Deutsches_Museum.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Dieselmotor_vs.jpg/500px-Dieselmotor_vs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Dieselmotor_vs.jpg/1280px-Dieselmotor_vs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Dieselmotor_vs.jpg/500px-Dieselmotor_vs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An MAN DM trunk piston diesel engine built in 1906. The MAN DM series is considered to be one of the first commercially successful diesel engines.[69]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADieselmotor_vs.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Fairbanks_Morse_model_32.jpg/500px-Fairbanks_Morse_model_32.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Fairbanks_Morse_model_32.jpg/500px-Fairbanks_Morse_model_32.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fairbanks Morse model 32","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFairbanks_Morse_model_32.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/ZT_303_Motor.jpg/500px-ZT_303_Motor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/ZT_303_Motor.jpg/1280px-ZT_303_Motor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/ZT_303_Motor.jpg/500px-ZT_303_Motor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Piston of an MAN M-System centre sphere combustion chamber type diesel engine (4 VD 14,5/12-1 SRW)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AZT_303_Motor.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/OM_352.jpg/500px-OM_352.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/OM_352.jpg/1280px-OM_352.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/OM_352.jpg/500px-OM_352.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mercedes-Benz OM 352, one of the first direct injected Mercedes-Benz diesel engines. It was introduced in 1963, but mass production only started in summer 1964.[117]","link":"https:/